\name{csemapp-package}
\alias{csemapp-package}
\alias{csemapp}
\docType{package}
\title{csemapp: A Point-and-Click Interface for PLS-SEM with 'cSEM'}
\description{
Ships the 'cSEM GUI' Shiny application, a graphical interface for partial
least squares structural equation modelling built on the \pkg{cSEM}
package. Start it with \code{\link{run_csem_gui}()}; read the step-by-step guide with
\code{\link{csem_gui_guide}()}.
}
\section{Main features}{
\itemize{
\item Drag-and-drop model builder (constructs, paths, moderators, quadratic effects)
\item PLS and consistent PLS (PLSc) estimation
\item Bootstrapping with parallel workers
\item Importance-performance map analysis (IPMA)
\item Confirmatory tetrad analysis (CTA)
\item PLSpredict and CVPAT (k-fold cross-validated prediction)
\item Results diagram and cSEM-style report tables with Excel export
}
}
